<title>SWEDEN: SCA 1996 profit falls 38 pct.</title>
<headline>SCA 1996 profit falls 38 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to December 31, 1996,</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items	     3,573    vs    5,731</p>
<p> Net sales			     55,405    vs   65,317</p>
<p> Earnings per share		   10.71    vs    17.55</p>
<p> Proposed dividend (crowns)	  5.25    vs     4.75</p>
<p> Operating costs			47,281   vs   54,858</p>
<p> Depreciation			    3,575   vs    3,581</p>
<p> Interests in associates		  32   vs	472</p>
<p> Operating profit			4,581   vs    7,350</p>
<p> Net financial items		   1,008   vs    1,619</p>
<p> Minorities				  312   vs	352</p>
<p> Tax					 1,144   vs    1,915</p>
<p>Return on shareholders' equity</p>
<p>				 (pct)	  10   vs	 17</p>
<p>NOTE -- Analysts polled by Reuters expected SCA to post a profit of 3.52 billion crowns after financial items. Full name of Swedish forestry company is Svenska Cellulosa Aktiebolaget SCA.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
